op left corner, flash and microphone, Apple logo in the middle, action and volume button featured slides over a giant text saying PRO cite26†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, partial side view, burgundy color, featuring a camera system with three lenses in the top left corner, flash and microphone, Apple logo in the middle, action and volume button featured slides over a giant text saying PRO L53: ## Switch to iPhone.\nL54: \nL55:   * ### Getting Started\nL56: \nL57: Switching from Android to iPhone is simple.\nL58: \nL59: cite27†Image: Hands exchanging phones, Android on the left without box, new iPhone 18 Pro, burgundy color (dark red), in box, on the right cite27†Image: Hands exchanging phones, Android on the left without box, new iPhone 18 Pro, burgundy color (dark red), in box, on the right L60: \nL61: ## Getting Started\nL62: \nL63: ### Switching from\nL64: Android\nL65: to iPhone\nL66: is simple.\nL67: #### Transfer your data in a few easy steps.\nL68: \nL69: Simply download the Move to iOS app on your Android phone to securely transfer the stuff you care about most to your iPhone — contacts, messages, WhatsApp content, photos, videos, email accounts, favorite apps, call history, and more.\nL70: \nL71: cite28†Learn more about the Move to iOS app†support.apple.com L72: cite29†Image: Android device on left, iPhone on right. Android device displays the Move to iOS App, with Select Items to Transfer heading and Messages, Contacts, and Call History Selected. iPhone screen shows Transfer Complete. cite29†Image: Android device on left, iPhone on right. Android device displays the Move to iOS App, with Select Items to Transfer heading and Messages, Contacts, and Call History Selected. iPhone screen shows Transfer Complete. L73: #### Continue your conversations with friends.\nL74: \nL75: Messages lets you reply with a quick emoji, create Memoji, and pay a friend for pizza. RCS (Rich Communication Services) messaging brings richer media and delivery and read receipts for those who don’t use iMessage.cite30†* And you can keep your conversations going on apps such as WhatsApp and WeChat.\nL76: cite31†Image: iPhone screen open to Messages app. Screen shows text conversation between two people that includes a Memoji. cite31†Image: iPhone screen open to Messages app. Screen shows text conversation between two people that includes a Memoji. L77: #### Everything just works.\nL78: \nL79: Apple engineers design our hardware and software together for a totally seamless experience. Want to connect your new AirPods to your iPhone? It’s a simple one‑tap setup. Want to share photos or contacts with friends nearby? AirDrop lists their names onscreen, so you can choose with a tap.\nL80: cite32†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Apple Music app with Home Screen open, next to AirPods Pro 3 in open MagSafe Charging case cite32†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Apple Music app with Home Screen open, next to AirPods Pro 3 in open MagSafe Charging case L81: #### Help is just a call or chat away.\nL82: \nL83: There are lots of ways to reach someone if you have questions. Call a Specialist, chat with someone online, go into an Apple Store, or use the Apple Support app. And the Tips app will help you get the most out of your iPhone over time.\nL84: \nL85: cite33†Image: Apple Specialist smiling with an approachable demeanor cite33†Image: Apple Specialist smiling with an approachable demeanor L86: \nL87:   * ### Designed to Last\nL88: \nL89: iPhone holds its value longer than other smartphones.\nL90: cite34†Image: iPhone Duo, Star White color, complete back exterior, Apple logo in center, 48MP Dual Fusion camera system, partial front interior, photo library displayed on screen cite34†Image: iPhone Duo, Star White color, complete back exterior, Apple logo in center, 48MP Dual Fusion camera system, partial front interior, photo library displayed on screen L91: ## Designed to Last\nL92: \nL93: ### iPhone holds its value longer\nL94: than other smartphones.\nL95: #### Innovative and durable.\nL96: \nL97: iPhone is protected by Ceramic Shield, which is tougher than any smartphone glass or glass ceramic. Our latest iPhone models have Ceramic Shield 2 on the front, with better scratch resistance,^{cite35†1 } and Ceramic Shield on the back for added durability. Little spill? No biggie — iPhone stands up to splashes from everyday liquids like water, coffee, and soda.^{cite36†2 }\nL98: cite37†Image: iPhone 17 horizontal on its side in lavender finish, with a layered design showcasing Ceramic Shield 2 cite37†Image: iPhone 17 horizontal on its side in lavender finish, with a layered design showcasing Ceramic Shield 2 L99: #### New now. And later.\nL100: \nL101: Regular iOS updates keep your iPhone feeling new for years to come. Just turn on automatic updates, and your iPhone stays current with the latest features and security.\nL102: cite38†Image: Four iPhone 18 Pro models, close-up front exteriors, each displaying various iOS features.\nL103: From left to right, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displaying a team debrief being scheduled by Siri AI, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displaying the Siri App, grid of cards representing past interactions, featuring topics like “Healthy 30 Minute Recipes,” “Mexico City Largest Park” with an accompanying image, and “Social Media Launch Email”, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displays an active phone call with “Passenger Airways” with a Call Context card on the bottom of the screen with relevant flight confirmation details, including the booking code, route from ORD to BCN, and flight times, with a note indicating the information was “Found in Mail”, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displays a conversation with Siri AI, asking about the color of a tablecloth. cite38†Image: Four iPhone 18 Pro models, close-up front exteriors, each displaying various iOS features.\nL104: From left to right, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displaying a team debrief being scheduled by Siri AI, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displaying the Siri App, grid of cards representing past interactions, featuring topics like “Healthy 30 Minute Recipes,” “Mexico City Largest Park” with an accompanying image, and “Social Media Launch Email”, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displays an active phone call with “Passenger Airways” with a Call Context card on the bottom of the screen with relevant flight confirmation details, including the booking code, route from ORD to BCN, and flight times, with a note indicating the information was “Found in Mail”, iPhone 18 Pro, screen displays a conversation with Siri AI, asking about the color of a tablecloth. L105: #### Supersmart, superspeedy Apple silicon.\nL106: \nL107: The vapor-cooled A20 Pro chip is the most powerful and efficient chip ever in an iPhone. And because it’s purpose-built for AI, with Neural Accelerators and a new Dual 16-core Neural Engine, A20 Pro supercharges everything from image generation to intelligent camera features.\nL108: cite39†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, demonstrating the performance capabilities of the A20 Pro chip with a scene from Monster Hunter Outlanders cite39†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, demonstrating the performance capabilities of the A20 Pro chip with a scene from Monster Hunter Outlanders L109: \nL110:   * ### Cutting-Edge Cameras\nL111: \nL112: Picture your best\nL113: photos and videos.\nL114: cite40†Image: Close-up image of iPhone 18 Pro camera lens, Burgundy color cite40†Image: Close-up image of iPhone 18 Pro camera lens, Burgundy color L115: ## Cutting-Edge Cameras\nL116: \nL117: ### Picture your best\nL118: photos and videos.\nL119: #### Stunning made simple.\nL120: \nL121: The advanced cameras in iPhone automatically capture phenomenal photos with great detail and color. And on iPhone Duo, Smart Take uses on-device AI to detect when people are posed and automatically takes the picture.\nL122: cite41†Image: iPhone Duo, opened in a horizontal position, series of iPhone photos side by side on both screens, close-up of a child and and three adults smiling with a birthday cake. cite41†Image: iPhone Duo, opened in a horizontal position, series of iPhone photos side by side on both screens, close-up of a child and and three adults smiling with a birthday cake. L123: #### Eye-opening control.\nL124: \nL125: With variable aperture on the 48MP Fusion Main camera, iPhone 18 Pro offers our best-ever camera system for pros and creators. It automatically adjusts depth of field for exceptional low-light photos and video. And with new Pro controls and Photographic Styles 3 to adjust texture and grain, you’ll have even more creative range.\nL126: cite42†Image: Series of iPhone photos, a person in a white jacket standing against a concrete wall, a close up of a woman leaning against a table with a shadow-filled room in the background, wide-angle shot of a person posing against a modern, colorful, architectural background, wide-angle shot of grassy mountains with purple flowers in the foreground, a woman posing on a set of stairs with the sun shining on her, a wide-angle shot of a starry night sky cite42†Image: Series of iPhone photos, a person in a white jacket standing against a concrete wall, a close up of a woman leaning against a table with a shadow-filled room in the background, wide-angle shot of a person posing against a modern, colorful, architectural background, wide-angle shot of grassy mountains with purple flowers in the foreground, a woman posing on a set of stairs with the sun shining on her, a wide-angle shot of a starry night sky L127: #### Make movies like the movies.\nL128: \nL129: Get pro-level videos using 4K 120 fps Dolby Vision on iPhone Duo and the latest Pro models. Use Action mode to steady shaky scenes as you shoot. Remove unwanted background noise from voices and music with Audio Mix. Add Cinematic mode effects, even after you shoot. Quickly access camera tools with Camera Control. And with the Center Stage front camera, use Dual Capture to record on front and rear cameras simultaneously.^{cite43†6 }\nL130: cite44†Image: Two young filmmakers direct a scene to group of young people using an iPhone 18 Pro in Glacier color mounted on a tripod cite44†Image: Two young filmmakers direct a scene to group of young people using an iPhone 18 Pro in Glacier color mounted on a tripod L131: \nL132:   * ### Apple Intelligence and Siri AI\nL133: \nL134: Helpful in all the\nL135: right places.\nL136: cite45†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, Burgundy color, partial front exterior, display screen shows conversation with Siri AI using Apple Intelligence, calendar app displayed below an iMessage about a deck treatment cite45†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, Burgundy color, partial front exterior, display screen shows conversation with Siri AI using Apple Intelligence, calendar app displayed below an iMessage about a deck treatment L137: ## Apple Intelligence and Siri AI\nL138: \nL139: ### Helpful in all the right places.\nL140: #### Just ask Siri AI.\nL141: \nL142: Your AI assistant, Siri AI is powered by Apple Intelligence and is more helpful than ever.^{cite46†3 } Get more done every day with richer answers, natural conversations, and a new, dedicated app. It’s truly helpful AI that’s centered around you and your needs — integrated into your apps, grounded in your context, and private at every step.\nL143: \nL144: Siri AI is rolling out in English.\nL145: Usage limits may apply.\nL146: cite47†Image: iPhone Duo, closed, Siri AI notification indicating a calendar update on outer display cite47†Image: iPhone Duo, closed, Siri AI notification indicating a calendar update on outer display L147: #### Start a visual search with the Shutter button.\nL148: \nL149: Siri mode in Camera and Visual Intelligence let you search, ask questions, and take action based on what’s around you with just a tap.^{cite48†4 }\nL150: cite49†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Siri mode in Camera being used to provide nutritional information about a bowl of chicken pho with noodles, veggies, and broth cite49†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Siri mode in Camera being used to provide nutritional information about a bowl of chicken pho with noodles, veggies, and broth L151: #### Next-level intelligent photo editing.\nL152: \nL153: Easy-to-use AI editing tools like Spatial Reframing let you adjust a shot after it’s been taken. You can expand your photos with the Extend tool. And remove objects with the enhanced Clean Up tool.^{cite50†5 }\nL154: cite51†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Spatial Reframing being used to reframe a close-up photo of a person with red roses behind her cite51†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Spatial Reframing being used to reframe a close-up photo of a person with red roses behind her L155: \nL156:   * ### Environment\nL157: \nL158: Designed with the earth in mind.\nL159: cite52†Image: iPhone Air in Space Black finish, back exterior showcasing Fusion camera system, 2-in-1 lens, LiDAR, flash and microphone cite52†Image: iPhone Air in Space Black finish, back exterior showcasing Fusion camera system, 2-in-1 lens, LiDAR, flash and microphone L160: ## Environment\nL161: \nL162: ### Designed with the earth in mind.\nL163: #### More recycled content? Naturally.\nL164: \nL165: We’re significantly expanding the use of key recycled metals in iPhone batteries, magnets, and circuit boards. Case in point: All our batteries are now made from 100 percent recycled cobalt.^{cite53†7 }\nL166: cite54†Image: iPhone Air, sky blue color, back exterior, MagSafe Battery attached, centered between a green recycling symbol and six small green circles arranged in a circle cite54†Image: iPhone Air, sky blue color, back exterior, MagSafe Battery attached, centered between a green recycling symbol and six small green circles arranged in a circle L167: #### Planet-worthy packaging.\nL168: \nL169: All iPhone packaging is made of paper that is 100 percent fiber based and can be easily recycled.\nL170: \nL171: cite55†Image: New iPhone box cite55†Image: New iPhone box L172: #### Apple Trade In.\nL173: \nL174: When you’re ready to buy a new iPhone, you can trade in your current iPhone or Android device and apply any credit toward your purchase. If your device isn’t eligible for credit, we’ll recycle it for free.\nL175: \nL176: cite56†Image: Hands exchanging trade-in iPhone 17 with Silicon cover, for new iPhone 18 Pro in the box. cite56†Image: Hands exchanging trade-in iPhone 17 with Silicon cover, for new iPhone 18 Pro in the box. L177: #### Innovation in conservation.\nL178: \nL179: Our disassembly robots — Daisy, Dave, and Taz — recover crucial materials like gold, cobalt, tungsten, and rare earth elements so they can be recycled and used again.\nL180: \nL181: cite57†Image: The futuristic hand and arm of one of Apple's pioneering disassembly robots. cite57†Image: The futuristic hand and arm of one of Apple's pioneering disassembly robots. L182: #### On track to carbon neutral.\nL183: \nL184: Our stores, offices, and data centers are already carbon neutral. By 2030, we aim to reach carbon neutrality for our global footprint.\nL185: \nL186: cite58†Image: Apple store at night, glass windows, lit up inside, Apple logo centered on top of front door. cite58†Image: Apple store at night, glass windows, lit up inside, Apple logo centered on top of front door. L187: \nL188:   * ### Privacy\nL189: \nL190: Your data.\nL191: Just where you want it.\nL192: cite59†Image: Silver Apple Privacy logo cite59†Image: Silver Apple Privacy logo L193: ## Privacy\nL194: \nL195: ### Your data.\nL196: Just where you want it.\nL197: #### Groundbreaking privacy protections.\nL198: \nL199: Apple Intelligence is integrated into your iPhone through on-device processing. So it’s aware of your personal information without collecting your personal information. With Private Cloud Compute, it can draw on larger, Apple-designed server-based models, running on Apple silicon, to handle more complex requests while protecting your privacy.\nL200: cite60†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Siri AI activated on screen cite60†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Siri AI activated on screen L201: #### Sign in safely.\nL202: \nL203: The Passwords app makes it easier to access account passwords, passkeys, Wi‑Fi passwords, and two-factor authentication codes stored securely on your device or synced with iCloud Keychain.\nL204: \nL205: cite61†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Passwords app displayed on screen cite61†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Passwords app displayed on screen L206: #### Browse securely.\nL207: \nL208: Private Browsing in Safari locks browsing windows when they’re not being used, blocks known trackers from loading on pages, and removes tracking added to URLs as you browse.\nL209: \nL210: cite62†Image: Person holding iPhone Air in sky blue finish in front of his face showing back exterior, dual camera system on left top corner cite62†Image: Person holding iPhone Air in sky blue finish in front of his face showing back exterior, dual camera system on left top corner L211: #### Share privately.\nL212: \nL213: All messages sent with iMessage use end-to-end encryption between devices, so they’re only seen by those you send them to. And Mail Privacy Protection hides your IP address, so senders can’t determine your location.\nL214: #### Pay the Apple Pay way.\nL215: \nL216: When you make a purchase with Apple Pay, your card numbers are never stored on your device or on Apple servers — and they’re never shared by Apple with merchants, either.\nL217: \nL218: cite63†Image: Partial iPhone screen display, showing a credit card being used in Apple Pay cite63†Image: Partial iPhone screen display, showing a credit card being used in Apple Pay L219: \nL220:   * ### Peace of Mind\nL221: \nL222: Helpful features.\nL223: On and off the grid.\nL224: cite64†Image: Overhead zoomed-out photo of Earth from space with satellite icon cite64†Image: Overhead zoomed-out photo of Earth from space with satellite icon L225: ## Peace of Mind\nL226: \nL227: ### Helpful features.\nL228: On and off the grid.\nL229: #### Out of range. Not out of reach.\nL230: \nL231: Unique safety features allow iPhone to connect to satellite frequencies — so you can send and receive messages via satellite, text emergency services, or get roadside assistance when you don’t have cell service or Wi‑Fi.^{cite65†8 }\nL232: cite66†Image: Three iPhone models side by side, display showing Messages, Find My, Roadside Assistance widgets available via Satellite, iPhone screen showing Emergency SOS in use, iPhone screen showing Roadside Assistance in use cite66†Image: Three iPhone models side by side, display showing Messages, Find My, Roadside Assistance widgets available via Satellite, iPhone screen showing Emergency SOS in use, iPhone screen showing Roadside Assistance in use L233: #### Everyday reassurance.\nL234: \nL235: With Find My, you can securely share your location with friends and family. And in Messages, you can use Check In to automatically let someone know when you’ve reached your destination safely.\nL236: \nL237: cite67†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Messages app open with Check In feature notifying recipient that the sender has arrived home cite67†Image: iPhone 18 Pro, front exterior, Messages app open with Check In feature notifying recipient that the sender has arrived home L238: ## Explore the lineup.\nL239: \nL240:   * cite20†Compare all models L241: \nL242:   * ### New iPhone Duo\nL243: \nL244:     *     * The largest display of any iPhone. Foldable. Posable. And durable.\nL245: \nL246:  ^{cite68†9 }\nL247: iPhone Duo^{cite69†◊ }\nL248: \nL249: cite14†Learn more cite23†View pricing L250: \nL251:   * ### New iPhone 18 Pro\nL252: \nL253:     *     *     *     * The ultimate performance and camera of any iPhone, with exceptional battery life.\nL254: \nL255:  ^{cite68†9 }\nL256: iPhone 18 Pro^{cite69†◊ }\nL257: \nL258: cite15†Learn more cite25†Buy L259: \nL260:   * ### iPhone Air\nL261: \nL262:     *     *     *     * Incredibly light and thin with pro performance.\nL263:  ^{cite68†9 }\nL264: iPhone Air^{cite69†◊ }\nL265: \nL266: cite16†Learn more cite70†Buy L267: \nL268:   * ### iPhone 17\nL269: \nL270:     *     *     *     *     * Powerful, durable, and delightful.\nL271: \nL272:  ^{cite68†9 }\nL273: iPhone 17^{cite69†◊ }\nL274: \nL275: cite17†Learn more cite71†Buy L276: \nL277:   * ### iPhone 17e\nL278: \nL279:     *     *     * Feature stacked.\nL280: Value packed.\nL281: \nL282:  ^{cite68†9 }\nL283: iPhone 17e^{cite69†◊ }\nL284: \nL285: cite18†Learn more cite72†Buy L286: \nL287:   * ### iPhone 16\nL288: \nL289:     *     *     *     *     * Amazing performance.\nL290: Durable design.\nL291: \nL292: ^{cite68†9 }\nL293: \nL294: cite73†Learn more cite19†Buy L295: ## Why Apple is the best\nL296: place to shop iPhone.\nL297: \nL298:   * cite13†Shop iPhone L299: \nL300:   * ### Apple Upgrade\nL301: \nL302: Love it. Lease it. Upgrade it.\nL303: \nL304: Lease a new iPhone with low monthly payments for 12 or 24 months and upgrade at the end of your term.^{cite74†§ }\nL305: cite75†Image: iPhone 17 Pro, Silver color, back exterior, 48MP Pro Fusion camera system, Apple logo in center, phone model overlaid on Apple Upgrade rosette in purple and red cite75†Image: iPhone 17 Pro, Silver color, back exterior, 48MP Pro Fusion camera system, Apple logo in center, phone model overlaid on Apple Upgrade rosette in purple and red L306: \nL307:   * ### Carrier Deals at Apple\nL308: \nL309: Get up to $1200 in credit on a new iPhone after trade‑in.\nL310: Includes carrier credits. AT&T: up to $1200. T‑Mobile: up to $1000. Verizon: up to $840.^{cite76†10 }\nL311: \nL312: cite77†Image: Verizon, AT&T, T- mobile cite77†Image: Verizon, AT&T, T- mobile L313: \nL314:   * ### Apple Trade In\nL315: \nL316: Save on a new iPhone with a trade‑in.\nL317: \nL318: Get credit toward your next iPhone when you trade in an eligible device.cite78†** L319: cite79†Image: Hands exchanging trade-in iPhone 17 with Silicon cover, for new iPhone 18 Pro in the box. cite79†Image: Hands exchanging trade-in iPhone 17 with Silicon cover, for new iPhone 18 Pro in the box. L320: ## Apple Trade In\nL321: ### Trade in your eligible device for credit.\nL322: \nL323: Just add a trade‑in when you choose a new product. Once your eligible device has been received and verified, we’ll credit the value to your payment method. Or choose to check out with Apple Card Monthly Installments and we’ll apply the credit instantly. Terms apply.\nL324: \nL325: cite80†Learn more L326: \nL327:   * ### Ways to Buy\nL328: \nL329: Pay over time, interest‑free.\nL330: \nL331: When you choose to check\nL332: out at Apple with Apple Card Monthly Installments.^{cite81†11 }\nL333: cite82†Image: Front of Apple Card, titanium finish cite82†Image: Front of Apple Card, titanium finish L334: ## Ways to Buy\nL335: ### Apple Card Monthly Installments.\nL336: \nL337: Pay for your new iPhone over time, interest‑free with Apple Card.^{cite81†11 } Simply choose to check out at Apple with Apple Card Monthly Installments as your payment option when you make your purchase. And enjoy 3% Daily Cash back, all up front. Terms apply.\nL338: \nL339: cite83†Learn more L340: \nL341:   * ### Personal Setup\nL342: \nL343: Meet your new iPhone with Personal Setup.\nL344: \nL345: Jump into online sessions with a Specialist to set up your iPhone and discover new features.\nL346: cite84†Image: Apple devices and features, iCloud, iPhone with Face ID and charging cable, Camera, Messages. cite84†Image: Apple devices and features, iCloud, iPhone with Face ID and charging cable, Camera, Messages. L347: ## Personal Setup\nL348: ### Jump into online, one‑on‑one sessions.\nL349: \nL350: When you buy your new iPhone directly from Apple, you’ll get access to Personal Setup. In these guided online sessions, a Specialist can walk you through setup and data transfer or focus on features that help you make the most of your iPhone. Best of all, you can join whenever works for you, from wherever you are.\nL351: \nL352: cite85†Learn more L353: \nL354:   * ### Delivery and Pickup\nL355: \nL356: Get flexible delivery\nL357: and easy pickup.\nL358: Choose two‑hour delivery from an Apple Store, free delivery, or easy pickup options.\nL359: \nL360: cite86†Image: Apple shopping bag in white color with Apple Logo near top cite86†Image: Apple shopping bag in white color with Apple Logo near top L361: ## Delivery and Pickup\nL362: ### Flexible delivery and pickup options.\nL363: \nL364: Get your new Apple products quickly and easily with two‑hour delivery from an Apple Store, free next‑day delivery, or convenient Apple pickup options.\nL365: \nL366: cite87†Learn more L367: \nL368:   * ### Guided Shopping\nL369: \nL370: Shop live with a Specialist.\nL371: \nL372: Let us help you find what you need and answer all of your questions, one on one, at an Apple Store or online.\nL373: cite88†Image: Apple Specialist smiling with an approachable demeanor cite88†Image: Apple Specialist smiling with an approachable demeanor L374: ## Guided Shopping\nL375: ### Get help finding what’s right for you.\nL376: \nL377: Specialists are here to answer your questions about all things Apple. Shop one on one with an Apple Specialist live, at an Apple Store or online.\nL378: \nL379: cite89†Shop with a Specialist online†contactretail.apple.com L380: \nL381:   * ### Apple Store App\nL382: \nL383: Explore a shopping experience designed around you.\nL384: \nL385: Use the Apple Store app to get a more personal way to shop.\nL386: \nL387: cite90†Image: Apple Store App, shopping bag icon, blue cite90†Image: App